{
	title: 'rm -rf of scratch paths runs without approval',
	spec: 'Setting scratch (text, optional, default empty) holds space-separated glob patterns (Bun.Glob, ~/ allowed) of scratch paths. rm -rf of a target matching one runs without approval, like targets inside /tmp. Targets expand as the shell does: unquoted ~/, and $VAR set earlier in the command to a literal absolute or ~/ path; a cd to such a path makes relative targets known as before. Targets with .., unknown variables, or quoted ~ still ask (.. may cross a symlink). Rationale: 34 of 44 rm -rf prompts in Oct 24 - Nov 12 histories were for disposable scratch dirs; host-specific patterns live in the gitignored config.ason.',
	status: 'done',
	needs: ['6f', 'pc'],
	foldInto: ['6f']
}
